 the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle went to 193% of normal in May to June and fell to 39% in November to December. Grid 16673 had its driest year in 2007 at 50% of normal. A preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 on grid 16673 sits at 69.6, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
